    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: default `registrationDate` to the server's current date\n\nWhen an owner is created without a `registrationDate`, the server now sets it to today's date and returns it in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format. A supplied date is preserved as-is.\n\n### Files changed\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` is `allOf` OwnerFields, it's accepted on `POST /api/owners` and returned on `GET /api/owners/{id}`. `format: date` makes the generated DTO field a `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` column, plus its getter/setter and the `java.time.LocalDate` import. MapStruct auto-maps it in both directions (entity \u21c4 DTO).\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, after mapping the incoming fields, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when it's null. (Update/other paths are untouched, matching the spec's scope of \"when no registration date is supplied.\")\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/mysql`, `db/postgres` `schema.sql`) \u2014 Added a nullable `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\n5. **`src/main/resources/db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 The seed owner rows used positional `INSERT ... VALUES`, so I appended a `NULL` for the new column. (The h2/postgres seeds already use explicit column lists and needed no change.)\n\n### Tests\nThe full suite (the `AcceptanceTest` class, including `coreDefaultsToToday` and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) passes: **Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0** \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
